  "notes": [
    "imd_decile is the 2019 vintage of each nation's index (IoD 2019, WIMD 2019, SIMD 2020v2, NIMDM 2017): the FRS 2024-25 variables IMDE, IMDW, IMDS and IMDN carry no change note from 2023-24, which predates the 2025 indices, and on an internal comparison England's FRS decile shares by region fit IoD 2019 better than IoD 2025, as the 2023-24 FRS does. The vintage is still to be confirmed with DWP.",
    "An area's decile is the one most of its live small-user postcodes carry in the May 2026 NSPL (oa21cd: the 2021 output area in England and Wales, the 2022 output area in Scotland, the 2021 data zone in Northern Ireland). Ranks are within-nation only.",
    "Northern Ireland's SOAs (2001) do not nest in its 2021 data zones, so many data zones' postcodes span deciles; the modal decile is recorded with relation inferred_modal and the counts below.",
    "England and Wales band weights read each area's LSOA mix as committed (shares to 6 dp ending at exactly 1), so households x share x 10^6 is exact. Scotland's read its 2022 data zone's dwellings by band, rounded half to even per band.",
    "Scotland's band mix is its 2022 data zone's, in which its 2022 output areas nest, at December 2024: nearest the FRS 2024-25 year and VOA's stock at 31 March 2025. NRS counts dwellings on the valuation list, as VOA does in England and Wales. Chronicle emits the zones' totals and bands A to H as facts (record set nrs.dwellings_data_zone_2025.2024, chronicle#421); this tool reads them from the pinned UK feed and records their fingerprint."
  ],
